Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:25:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add interactive Desmos graphs to the complex numbers post

Adds two "try it yourself" iframe embeds (vector addition, and
multiplication as rotate+scale) alongside their existing static SVG
diagrams, so readers can manipulate the ideas directly. Each embed
points at a graph authored on desmos.com and is a supplement, not a
replacement, so the explanation still stands if the embed is slow,
blocked, or JS is off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018vfDmGbUETokYVrrgvpv1J
---
 DESIGN.md                                  |  1 +
 blog/complex-numbers-visual-intuition.html | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/DESIGN.md b/DESIGN.md
index c926532..454c54e 100644
--- a/DESIGN.md
+++ b/DESIGN.md
@@ -297,6 +297,7 @@ Two radius scales doing two different jobs: a tight 3px on every interactive con
 - **Diagram Figure:** Soft Cream background, 1px Sand Border, 10px radius, capped at 440px wide and centered, holding one hand-authored inline SVG plus a caption. Diagram SVGs use the palette's literal hex values directly (not `var()`) since they're static illustrations, not interactive UI needing live theme response. Caption text reuses the existing `caption` type token (0.76rem, Muted) rather than introducing a new size.
 - **Worked-Algebra Box** (`.demo`): White background, 4px Warm Terracotta Deep left border, 10px radius. This mirrors the `ldmexample` terracotta convention from the LaTeX student-notes system (`Notes/template/lukedoesmaths.sty`) — terracotta already means "worked example" in the brand's other medium, so the web picks up the same color-to-meaning mapping rather than inventing a new one. The label line uses Terracotta Deep (never plain terracotta) per the Read-It-Or-Fill-It Rule.
 - **Closing Callout Box** (`.callout`): Soft Cream background, 4px Chalkboard Teal left border, 10px radius. Mirrors the LaTeX system's `ldmsummary` teal side-rule ("key points" / reminder convention) — used here for the one closing note per post that visual intuition supports but doesn't replace algebraic practice.
+- **Interactive Embed** (`.desmos-embed`): Same Soft Cream/Sand Border/10px-radius family as the Diagram Figure, but capped wider (640px vs. 440px) since an interactive graph's sliders and drag targets need more room than a static illustration to stay usable. Labeled with the same "Try it yourself" small-caps Terracotta Deep label as the worked-algebra boxes. This is the site's first embedded third-party content — unlike the hand-authored SVG diagrams, it's a plain `<iframe>` onto a graph authored directly on desmos.com, added as a supplement alongside a diagram rather than a replacement, so the explanation still stands if the embed is slow, blocked, or JS is off. Used on both the vector-addition diagram (section 3) and the rotate+scale diagram (section 4) of the complex numbers post.
 
 ## Do's and Don'ts
 
